# No local naming (this repo)

This repository is **public framework code**. Tests, fixtures, docs, and examples ship with it.

## Never commit

- Real client / product / portfolio names from the maintainer's machine
- Machine paths (personal home + `Work` checkouts)
- Hub distill content (`$MEMORY_HOME`, `.devhub/`, `chats/projects/<real>.md`)
- Encoded or obfuscated denylists of those real names (byte tuples, base64 of brands, etc.)

## Use instead

Fictional identifiers only, for example:

| Kind | Examples |
|------|----------|
| Project slug | `example-app`, `other-app`, `alpha-hub`, `beta-app`, `widget-ui` |
| User / home | `example-user`, `me`, `alice` (in synthetic paths only) |
| URL | `https://example.org/`, `https://example.com/` |
| Workspace encode | `Users-me-Work-example-app`, `-home-example-user-Work-example-app` |

Allowlist lives in `tests/test_no_hardcoded_paths.py` (`APPROVED_FICTIONAL`). Extend that set when you need a new generic name — do not invent one-off real brands.

## Enforcement

- CI: `tests/test_no_hardcoded_paths.py`
- Human: [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md) → **Generic plugin rule**
